{
 "name": "Fish",
 "title": "Low-poly fish",
 "description": "Perch-shaped fish traced from a side-view illustration: a skinned body on a four-bone spine, a forked tail, dorsal, anal, pelvic and pectoral fins. The dorsal and anal fins are skinned with the body's own bones and the pelvic fin is bound to the body surface, so every fin root moves with the surface it grows from and none of them slide or open a seam while swimming. Swim, Idle and Die (thrash, roll belly-up and float).",
 "ground": false,
