   "depth": 0.3,
   "height": 0.15,
   "width": 0.07,
   "tolerance": 0.08
  },
  "notes": "Trace: length/height 2.0 including fins. Body deepest at 55-65% of the length from the tail (body alone ~0.62 of the full height), caudal peduncle ~0.30, tail ~17% of the length. Laterally compressed: width ~45% of body height. Dorsal fin runs 30-75% of the length. Fin roots are pushed 4-6 mm inside the body contour (weld), not laid on the surface."
 },
